WEBVTT

00:00:00.723 --> 00:00:02.998
Central ideas and details.

00:00:02.998 --> 00:00:04.473
Subject plus claim.

00:00:04.473 --> 00:00:07.637
Not too narrow, not too broad, not too extreme.

00:00:09.177 --> 00:00:10.752
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:10.752 --> 00:00:13.702
The question asks for the main idea of the text.

00:00:13.702 --> 00:00:15.552
And the passage is short.

00:00:15.552 --> 00:00:18.129
Sometimes science, sometimes a story.

00:00:19.156 --> 00:00:22.969
It's testing whether you can separate the main point from the details.

00:00:24.011 --> 00:00:25.236
Here's the method.

00:00:25.236 --> 00:00:26.561
Find the subject.

00:00:26.561 --> 00:00:28.291
Who or what is this about?

00:00:28.291 --> 00:00:29.366
Find the claim.

00:00:29.366 --> 00:00:31.071
What does the author say about it?

00:00:31.071 --> 00:00:33.746
Watch for turn words like but and however.

00:00:33.746 --> 00:00:37.871
Predict the main idea in one sentence: subject plus claim.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.771
Then filter the choices.

00:00:39.771 --> 00:00:43.277
Cut anything too narrow, too broad, or too extreme.

00:00:44.318 --> 00:00:46.218
Use these four filters.

00:00:46.218 --> 00:00:49.673
Too narrow: one true detail, not the whole point.

00:00:49.673 --> 00:00:53.248
Too broad: it claims more than the passage covers.

00:00:53.248 --> 00:00:58.553
Too extreme: words like proves, always, or never, on a careful passage.

00:00:58.553 --> 00:01:02.167
And remember, the main point usually comes right after the turn.

00:01:03.214 --> 00:01:04.564
Let's try one.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:08.514
First comes the old view: scientists assumed plants were passive.

00:01:08.514 --> 00:01:09.964
Then the turn: however.

00:01:09.964 --> 00:01:12.614
Plants can detect signals, and respond.

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:14.439
That new view is the point.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:15.664
Now filter.

00:01:15.664 --> 00:01:18.139
C is one detail, so it's too narrow.

00:01:18.139 --> 00:01:19.789
D is too extreme.

00:01:19.789 --> 00:01:22.204
A is a basic fact, not the point.

00:01:22.204 --> 00:01:25.247
B captures the shift from passive to responsive.

00:01:26.306 --> 00:01:28.231
Watch out for the true detail.

00:01:28.231 --> 00:01:29.311
It's accurate.

00:01:29.311 --> 00:01:30.936
It's even in the passage.

00:01:30.936 --> 00:01:33.007
But it's only one piece of the point.

00:01:34.044 --> 00:01:35.924
Here's the lesson on one page.

00:01:35.924 --> 00:01:36.999
How to spot it.

00:01:36.999 --> 00:01:38.374
The four steps.

00:01:38.374 --> 00:01:39.509
The filters.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:40.534
And the trap.

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:43.295
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
